  "description": "This is a deposit for half the ALUMAX II frame and fork that will be ready to ship early 2027\n$2,200 is for the raw (pictured) finish. $120 extra for a powder coat of your choice.\n700x55 tire clearance. chains stays will be 5mm longer than pictured\nthe AluMax II is my built for speed modern grav racing bike interpretation designed to hold its own with anything your dental care provider would afford. New England made from 100% metal Italian materials.\n\n- Weights: large Frame: 1695g Taper Trax fork: 860g\n- complete bike weight of 21 lbs as pictured\n- frame made from Dedacciai 7005 Aluminum by Frank the Welder in Bellows Falls Vermont.\n- taper trax fork made from Columbus steel in Vermont\n- clearance for 700x55\n- cantilever or V brakes\n- QR 135 rear spacing and 100 front.\n- 68mm threaded english bb shell\n- 1 1/8\" steerer\n- 27.2 seatpost\n- 31.8 front der clamp and seat clamp\n- all external cable routing\n- no fender mounts this time\n- choice of powder coat or raw aluminum/steel\n- geometry comparisons to your current bike available on BIKE INSIGHTS\n\nsend me an email if you have any questions on this frame. ronnie@ronsbikes.com",
